{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>יִירַשׁ הַצְּלָצֵל.</b> From the root of (Deuteronomy 4:38) לְהוֹרִישׁ גּוֹיִם — and likewise its Targum is יִתְרֵךְ. And Rashi, of blessed memory, explained it from the root רֵישׁ, that is to say, it will make him poor of fruit. And the צְלָצֵל is a species of locust, and it is called צְלָצֵל on account of the noise they make when they come gathered together, from the root of (Psalms 150:5) בִּצְלְצְלֵי תְרוּעָה. And its Targum is סַקְיָא, from the language of the Rabbis: וְנָטְלוּהּ מַסִּיקִין, that is, robbers — because they rob the fruits and consume them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:41.514305716Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}